WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.902
-Trumpism lost badly

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.170
last night in California

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.739
when Governor Gavin Newsom
easily beat back

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:08.741
a GOP-led recall effort,

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:12.012
but Trumpism is still very much
the core of the modern GOP,

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.612
as evidenced
by how many Republicans

00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:16.115
still refuse to accept the
results of the 2020 election.

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:18.551
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:22.455
♪♪

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:25.457
If you weren't really following
the California recall election

00:00:25.457 --> 00:00:27.827
because it was too dumb
and confusing, you're not alone.

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:30.530
In fact, there were
three options on the ballot,

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.631 line:0%
that said...

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.735 line:0%
Seriously, why is getting
into LAX like such a nightmare?

00:00:36.735 --> 00:00:38.604
Most airports, you have
to get there two hours

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.139
before your flight, but at LAX,

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:42.475
you have to get to the entrance
of the airport

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.477
two hours before you need
to be inside the airport.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:47.146
You could drive to LAX,
or you could just

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:49.315
drive back to New York
in the same amount of time.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:52.051
Once, I was stuck in traffic,
waiting to get to departures

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:53.819
and I looked over
at the driver next to me

00:00:53.819 --> 00:00:55.221
and he was a skeleton.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.023
[ Laughter ]
Of course, in L.A.,

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.357
they don't call that a skeleton.

00:00:58.357 --> 00:00:59.826
They call that
a weight loss goal.

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:00.860
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.262
And even then,

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.562
even the fact
that it was a skeleton

00:01:03.562 --> 00:01:06.900
was less jarring to me
than the car he was driving.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.635
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:12.071
Can we see the skeleton car
one more time?

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:13.139
That's a good --

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.208
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.109
Go full frame.
Let's look at it full frame

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:18.411
one more time.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.479
Yeah.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.981
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.483
Speeding, going as fast
as they can.

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:26.986
We said to the graphics team,
"Put a skeleton in a car."

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.321
They go, "We know just the car!"

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:31.323
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.323 --> 00:01:33.993
You see, the key, the key,

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.996
the key to bypassing
all the traffic at LAX is

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.598
to get dropped off
at the arrivals

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:42.268
and then just take the escalator
upstairs to departures.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.103
An Uber driver
once told me that,

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:46.739
before he asked me
if I had any cocaine.

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.474
[ Laughter ]
In the immortal words
of Randy Newman,

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:50.209
"I love L.A.
I love it."

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:53.178
Anyway, the recall effort
was defeated so easily

00:01:53.178 --> 00:01:54.647
and called so quickly

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.149 line:0%
that MSNBC correspondent
Steve Kornacki

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:59.452 line:0%
didn't have much
to get worked up over.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.586 line:0%
-And there it is. You can see

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.354 line:0%
the news, Brian,
with the check mark.

00:02:02.354 --> 00:02:04.657 line:0%
NBC News is
officially projecting

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:07.326 line:0%
that the recall attempt
against Gavin Newsom,

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:09.862 line:0%
the governor of California,
has failed.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:11.697 line:0%
It's failing, as you can see
by the results here,

00:02:11.697 --> 00:02:13.165 line:0%
decisively, at this point.

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:17.036 line:0%
We now have 60% of all the vote
counted here in California.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.471 line:0%
The recall, right now,
is failing

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.473 line:0%
by a better than 2:1 margin.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:23.242 line:0%
The difference there is
2.7 million votes.

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.144 line:0%
That's a 35-point margin.

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:27.380 line:0%
It's clear,
from what we have right now,

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:28.747 line:0%
it's clear to our decision desk.

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:30.282 line:0%
I think it's clear to everybody
who's been watching

00:02:30.282 --> 00:02:32.451 line:0%
along with me here that this
number is going to come

00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:35.020 line:0%
nowhere near 50%.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.489 line:0%
This one is a landslide.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:37.790 line:0%
The recall fails.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:41.293 line:0%
Gavin Newsom is going to survive
as California's governor.

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:43.462
-Just must've been
so frustrating for Kornacki.

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:44.831
I mean, look at him.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:47.433
He might look like he's going
to teach you fractions,

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.436
but the man is
an adrenaline junkie.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.538
The batches of votes
from outlier counties,

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:54.740
the taste of disposable Bic ink,

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.276
the swishing of his khakis
as he darts to his map.

00:02:57.276 --> 00:03:00.046
Well, after an early election
call like that last night,

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.881
he probably had
to stop off at the OTB

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.549
on the way home for a fix.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:05.618
It is just a waste
to see Kornacki's talent

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.787
so underutilized
on a blowout election.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.688
It's like watching
a thoroughbred racehorse

00:03:09.688 --> 00:03:11.724
pull some tourists
through Central Park.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:14.059
[Hoarsely]
"I won the Triple Crown,
you know."

00:03:14.059 --> 00:03:17.197
[ Inhaling ]
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.898
They smoke through their
mouths, horses.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.666
[ Laughter ]
Now, in case you aren't aware,

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:24.470
recalls in California are,
to use a political insider term,

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.538
super [bleep] dumb.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.106
There are two questions
on the ballot --

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:29.642
one, asking if you want
to recall the governor;

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:32.345
and another,
asking who should replace him,

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.647
if the recall succeeds,
which means,

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.182
a sitting governor
could get recalled

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.649
if they get 49% of the vote

00:03:37.649 --> 00:03:40.653
and then, get replaced
by someone who got half that.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.756
It's insane. I mean, who came up
with this system, anyway?

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:46.325
Like M.C. Escher?
It's more complicated

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:47.660
than following
the latest developments

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.994
in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe.

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:51.397
We're at the point, now,
where this is true.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.098
This building 30 Rock,
the one we're in right now,

00:03:53.098 --> 00:03:55.435
is featured in the new
"Hawkeye" trailer,

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:59.339
which means I'm technically
canon in the MCU,

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:00.973
which I assume also means
I got blipped

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:02.374
for five years
in "Infinity War"

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:06.111
and -- oh, okay, so I guess
that's what that was.

00:04:06.111 --> 00:04:08.213
It would also explain why,
back in 2018,

00:04:08.213 --> 00:04:11.250
Wally disintegrated
in the middle of a show.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:15.321
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:18.491
[ Clapping ]

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:19.825
I get it.
You worked on that all day

00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:21.594
and you were like,
"We need a car!"

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:25.498
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:26.866
Of course, when that
happened to Wally,

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:29.001
we just assumed he was trying
to hide from his bookie

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:31.170
after he bet on the Yankees
to win the World Series.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.239
[ Laughter ]
Anyway --

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:35.908
Oh, they laugh when it's close
to the bone, Wally.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.244
[ Laughter ]
Anyway, so the recall system

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.279
is nuts
and it should be scrapped.

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:42.382
As the California secretary
of state put it...

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:47.453
A hundred years.

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:49.489
If something isn't working,

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:51.691
you don't give it 100 years.

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:54.193
I did a standing monologue
for about a year

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.462
and never figured out
where my hands go

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.464
and then, Shoemaker said,
"You know where they go?

00:04:58.464 --> 00:04:59.765
On a desk."

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:01.401
[ Laughter ]
We shouldn't be
running elections

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:03.770
on a system that is older
than the Cyclone.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:05.738
The Cyclone doesn't even
have any loops or twists,

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:06.939
just missing planks of wood.

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.674
The thrill comes
from seeing your life flash

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:10.576
before your eyes
before you get on.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:14.013
A priest administers last rites,
but it's not a real priest.

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:16.448
It's just like a high school
sophomore on summer vacation.

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:17.817
Although,
I guess it makes sense.

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.418
California's electoral system

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:21.254
is as complicated
as their highway system.

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:24.623
One time, I was trying to get
from Burbank to Santa Monica

00:05:24.623 --> 00:05:26.358
and my GPS killed itself.

00:05:26.358 --> 00:05:27.927
-I can't do this anymore.

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:29.461
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.461 --> 00:05:31.330
-Why is every electoral system
in this country

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.665
so backwards and insane?

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:35.068
Gerrymandering,
the Electoral College, recalls.

00:05:35.068 --> 00:05:37.002
Why can't there just be a winner

00:05:37.002 --> 00:05:38.838
who gets the most votes
and that's it?

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:41.140
Why is it easier to vote
in "America's Got Talent"

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.408
than it is to vote in America?

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:45.111
If Doritos chose
their flavors this way,

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:47.813
the top seller would be
cilantro &amp; cauliflower.

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:51.083
This dumb, waste-of-time recall
has already cost $276 million

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:54.020 line:0%
and could end up costing more
than $300 million,

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.756 line:0%
all because Newsom went
to dinner during the lockdowns

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:58.824 line:0%
at a fancy restaurant called
the French Laundry,

00:05:58.824 --> 00:06:00.859 line:0%
which, we can all agree,

00:06:00.859 --> 00:06:03.095 line:0%
was absolutely stupid,
on his part.

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:06.098 line:0%
It's like that restaurant
was named specifically

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:07.232 line:0%
to piss people off.

00:06:07.232 --> 00:06:09.902 line:0%
It's named after two things
everybody hates.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:11.037 line:0%
He might've gotten away with it

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:12.238 line:0%
if he'd gone
to a place called...

00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:15.541 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
I don't think --

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.009 line:0%
I don't think he should've
been recalled,

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:18.510 line:0%
but I do think they
should've punished him

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:19.879 line:0%
by passing a law stating

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:21.881 line:0%
the only dinner
he's allowed to have

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.349 line:0%
from now on is pizza from L.A.

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:25.384 line:0%
Have you ever had pizza in L.A.?
It's not even pizza.

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:27.853 line:0%
It's like an English muffin
with ketchup on it.

00:06:27.853 --> 00:06:30.823
Oh, but good news --
they deliver until about 7:30

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:33.926
[ Laughter ]
and they put weird [bleep]
on it, like seitan or avocado.

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.861
To this day, I think
California Pizza Kitchen

00:06:35.861 --> 00:06:38.296
was like "Springtime for Hitler"
in "The Producers."

00:06:38.296 --> 00:06:40.199
It was built to fail,

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:42.235
and then against all odds,
it was a hit.

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:43.435
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.435 --> 00:06:45.771
One time, I bought L.A.-style
pizza for my crew

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:47.940
and they threatened to dump
my body in the East River.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.375
Luckily, none of them
could lift me

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.010
because of their belly cramps.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.311
[ Laughter ]
[ New York accent ]
Barbecue sauce isn't supposed

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:54.213
to go with peaches!

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:57.183
[ Laughter ]
Point is --

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:58.818
It's really nice
when California's in the news

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:02.788
because we make a lot
of New York-centric jokes here.

00:07:02.788 --> 00:07:06.458
California, stop wasting money
on recalls, and fix your pizza.

00:07:06.458 --> 00:07:08.527
But it's also not surprising
that this was the way

00:07:08.527 --> 00:07:10.796
Republicans tried
to stage a takeover

00:07:10.796 --> 00:07:12.598
of the most populous state
in America,

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:13.966
not through a normal election,

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:15.968
but through a weird loophole
where they would only need

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.936
a small percentage
of voters to win.

00:07:17.936 --> 00:07:19.905
This is the same party
that's appointed

00:07:19.905 --> 00:07:22.541
a majority of the current
Supreme Court justices,

00:07:22.541 --> 00:07:25.343
yet, has only won
the national popular vote once

00:07:25.343 --> 00:07:26.779
in the last 32 years.

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:30.182
In 2012, they won control of the
House through gerrymandering,

00:07:30.182 --> 00:07:32.985
despite getting fewer
total votes than Democrats.

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:35.521
In the Senate,
there's currently a 50/50 tie,

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.256
despite the fact
that Democrats represent

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:39.025
41 million more Americans.

00:07:39.025 --> 00:07:41.026
In fact, Senate Republicans
haven't represented

00:07:41.026 --> 00:07:43.762
an actual majority of Americans
since 1996.

00:07:43.762 --> 00:07:47.799
The GOP's entire
political strategy is based

00:07:47.799 --> 00:07:49.268
on exploiting cheat codes,

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:51.070
rather than appealing
to a majority of voters,

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.138
like when
Mitch McConnell realized

00:07:53.138 --> 00:07:54.806
he could just manipulate
the filibuster

00:07:54.806 --> 00:07:56.708
to stonewall everything
Obama did

00:07:56.708 --> 00:08:00.580
and turn reconciliation --
an arcane budgetary tactic --

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.682
into the only vehicle
for passing legislation.

00:08:02.682 --> 00:08:03.982
They're like those kids
in middle school

00:08:03.982 --> 00:08:05.584
who would cheat
during "GoldenEye"

00:08:05.584 --> 00:08:07.153
by turning themselves
invincible

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:08.487
and you'd ask them
how they did it, and they say,

00:08:08.487 --> 00:08:11.757
"It's easy. You just do
L+down, R+C right,

00:08:11.757 --> 00:08:13.425
R+C up, L+right,

00:08:13.425 --> 00:08:15.161
L+C down, R+C up,

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:16.962
L+right, R+down,

00:08:16.962 --> 00:08:19.231
L+left+R+C right,"

00:08:19.231 --> 00:08:20.666
and then you'd spend
the rest of the game trying

00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:22.468
to figure it out and, while
you're not paying attention,

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:24.937
they'd eat
all the cauliflower Doritos.

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:27.473
Anyway, Newsom defeated
the recall easily.

00:08:27.473 --> 00:08:28.941
And, yet,
as he warned last night,

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:32.512
the forces that led to this
recall are not going away.

00:08:32.512 --> 00:08:36.515
-Just in the last,
you know, few days

00:08:36.515 --> 00:08:41.954
the former president put out,
saying this election was rigged.

00:08:41.954 --> 00:08:45.157
Democracy is not a football.

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:48.427
You don't throw it around.

00:08:48.427 --> 00:08:51.697
It's more like a, I don't know,
antique vase.

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:52.965
[ Laughter ]
You can drop it

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:55.868
and smash it in a million
different pieces.

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:58.904
And that's what we're
capable of doing,

00:08:58.904 --> 00:09:02.541
if we don't stand up to meet
the moment and push back.

00:09:02.541 --> 00:09:04.676
I said this many, many times

00:09:04.676 --> 00:09:07.580
on the campaign trail,
you know.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.081
We may have defeated Trump,

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:11.550
but Trumpism is not dead
in this country.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:14.186
-It's true -- Trump may be gone,
but Trumpism is not dead.

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:17.722
In fact, it is very much
the core of the modern GOP.

00:09:17.722 --> 00:09:19.892
We can't just plug our ears
and hope it'll go away,

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:22.228
like Larry David
at New York Fashion Week.

00:09:22.228 --> 00:09:24.496
[ Laughter ]
And you know, as a society,
we should force Larry David

00:09:24.496 --> 00:09:26.866
to attend more events he doesn't
want to go to for our amusement.

00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:28.834
It would be great to see him
at Burning Man

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:29.969
or Cirque du Soleil.

00:09:29.969 --> 00:09:31.636
[ As David ]
I...It's bad.

00:09:31.636 --> 00:09:33.472
I...It's a bad circus.

00:09:33.472 --> 00:09:35.607
[ Laughter ]
I don't care for the sad clowns.

00:09:35.607 --> 00:09:37.809
"You know, I actually was
the sad clown tonight, Larry."

00:09:37.809 --> 00:09:39.044
Oh.

00:09:39.044 --> 00:09:40.112
Can I ask you a question?

00:09:40.112 --> 00:09:41.580
[ Laughter ]

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:43.549
When you go
to the clown college,

00:09:43.549 --> 00:09:45.484
do they separate you
into funny or sad

00:09:45.484 --> 00:09:47.252
or, uhhh, do you choose it?

00:09:47.252 --> 00:09:49.188
"Well, they suggest
what clowning

00:09:49.188 --> 00:09:50.222
suits your strengths, yes."

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:52.258
Because you know,
it seems to me like, uh,

00:09:52.258 --> 00:09:55.694
a funny clown, little bit harder
than a sad clown.

00:09:55.694 --> 00:09:57.462
[ Laughter ]
"I don't think that's true
at all, Larry."

00:09:57.462 --> 00:09:59.899
I...think it'd be
a little bit easier.

00:09:59.899 --> 00:10:01.400
[ Laughter ]

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.002
One balloon, painted-on tear.

00:10:04.002 --> 00:10:06.071
Pretty, pretty
sure I could do it.

00:10:06.071 --> 00:10:08.640
[ Laughter ]
So, as the California recall --

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.008
I don't know
how that episode ends,

00:10:10.008 --> 00:10:11.677
but I think it's
with Larry David going --

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:13.545
[ As David ] Sad clown!
[ Laughter ]

00:10:13.545 --> 00:10:15.981
So, as the California recall
showed last night,

00:10:15.981 --> 00:10:18.817
Trumpism has real political cost
for the GOP,

00:10:18.817 --> 00:10:20.686
since it's massively unpopular.

00:10:20.686 --> 00:10:22.755
In this case,
it was a disaster for the GOP,

00:10:22.755 --> 00:10:23.856
but that doesn't mean it's dead.

00:10:23.856 --> 00:10:25.490
It's still very much alive.

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:28.593
It's the central animating force
of Republican politics.

00:10:28.593 --> 00:10:31.330
In fact, the same
insane conspiracy theories

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:32.664
about nonexistent fraud

00:10:32.664 --> 00:10:34.934
that Republicans circulated
about the 2020 election

00:10:34.934 --> 00:10:37.035
have circulated again
in California.

00:10:37.035 --> 00:10:40.038 line:0%
GOP frontrunner Larry Elder's
campaign pushed

00:10:40.038 --> 00:10:42.908 line:0%
baseless fraud claims before the
election even occurred

00:10:42.908 --> 00:10:44.543 line:0%
and, on the eve of the recall,

00:10:44.543 --> 00:10:46.579 line:0%
Elder tore a page
out of Trump's handbook

00:10:46.579 --> 00:10:49.648 line:0%
by refusing to say that he
would accept the results.

00:10:49.648 --> 00:10:51.016 line:0%
-Whether or not you win or lose,

00:10:51.016 --> 00:10:53.586 line:0%
will you accept the results
of the election tomorrow?

00:10:53.586 --> 00:10:56.422 line:0%
-I think we all ought to be
looking at election integrity,

00:10:56.422 --> 00:10:57.823 line:0%
no matter whether
you're a Democrat,

00:10:57.823 --> 00:10:59.324 line:0%
an Independent,
or a Republican.

00:10:59.324 --> 00:11:00.893 line:0%
-Is that a commitment
to accept the results

00:11:00.893 --> 00:11:02.561 line:0%
of the election tomorrow?
-Let's all do that together.

00:11:02.561 --> 00:11:05.097 line:0%
Let's all work together,
on both sides of the aisle,

00:11:05.097 --> 00:11:06.832 line:0%
to make sure that the election
is a fair election.

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:08.434 line:0%
-Is that a commitment
to accept the results

00:11:08.434 --> 00:11:09.901 line:0%
of the election tomorrow?
-Let's all work together

00:11:09.901 --> 00:11:11.303 line:0%
to find out whether or not

00:11:11.303 --> 00:11:13.172 line:0%
the election tomorrow
is a fair election.

00:11:13.172 --> 00:11:14.507 line:0%
Let's all work together
to do that.

00:11:14.507 --> 00:11:15.941 line:0%
-So that is not a commitment

00:11:15.941 --> 00:11:17.442 line:0%
to accept the results
of the election tomorrow?

00:11:17.442 --> 00:11:19.477 line:0%
-Boy, Jacob, honestly.

00:11:19.477 --> 00:11:20.779 line:0%
I answered your question.

00:11:20.779 --> 00:11:21.847 line:0%
Let's all work together.

00:11:21.847 --> 00:11:23.081 line:0%
We all should have
a vested interest

00:11:23.081 --> 00:11:25.650 line:0%
in making sure that the
election is a fair one

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:27.519 line:0%
and is one that was conducted
with integrity.

00:11:27.519 --> 00:11:28.887
-Why do you keep saying
all of us?

00:11:28.887 --> 00:11:30.656
The rest of us
already do believe

00:11:30.656 --> 00:11:32.258
elections are fair
because they are.

00:11:32.258 --> 00:11:34.560
Republicans talk
about nonexistent voter fraud

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.094
like the drunk guy
at the Houlihan's

00:11:36.094 --> 00:11:37.563
who ate too many spicy wings.

00:11:37.563 --> 00:11:39.631
"Damn it, guys!
The spicy wings

00:11:39.631 --> 00:11:41.733
made us all [bleep] our pants!

00:11:41.733 --> 00:11:44.670
We all need to go change
our pants together."

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:45.938
[ Laughter ]

00:11:45.938 --> 00:11:47.706 line:0%
As it turns out, that strategy

00:11:47.706 --> 00:11:49.141 line:0%
backfired big-time
on Republicans

00:11:49.141 --> 00:11:51.209 line:0%
and Elder ultimately conceded

00:11:51.209 --> 00:11:52.644 line:0%
after the polls closed
last night.

00:11:52.644 --> 00:11:54.313 line:0%
Nonetheless,
Elder had previously claimed

00:11:54.313 --> 00:11:55.947 line:0%
there might be shenanigans
in the election

00:11:55.947 --> 00:11:57.582
and Republicans
spent the campaign

00:11:57.582 --> 00:12:00.385
spreading the same old
bat[bleep] conspiracy theories

00:12:00.385 --> 00:12:02.954
about supposed voter fraud
they've spread in other states

00:12:02.954 --> 00:12:04.256
across the country.
For example...

00:12:19.738 --> 00:12:23.275
Of course, of course, Lindell
is somehow connected to this.

00:12:23.275 --> 00:12:24.877
The guy has inserted himself

00:12:24.877 --> 00:12:27.379
into every political story
of the last two years.

00:12:27.379 --> 00:12:31.150
It's like if Forrest Gump
had a louder, dumber brother.

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:33.352
[ As Lindell ]
I heard they've been
getting rid of ballots

00:12:33.352 --> 00:12:36.822
by going down to Santa Monica
and dumping them off

00:12:36.822 --> 00:12:38.257
da piers!

00:12:38.257 --> 00:12:39.691
[ Laughter ]

00:12:39.691 --> 00:12:40.993
Nice when a new one turns up.

00:12:40.993 --> 00:12:42.728
Every time
you think we're out...

00:12:42.728 --> 00:12:44.563
[ Laughter ]

00:12:44.563 --> 00:12:46.631
In fact, it's now become
a baseline requirement

00:12:46.631 --> 00:12:48.566
for aspiring
Republican politicians

00:12:48.566 --> 00:12:50.869
to insist that Trump actually
won the 2020 election

00:12:50.869 --> 00:12:53.972
and that any election
Republicans lose
is illegitimate.

00:12:53.972 --> 00:12:56.675
According to a new poll
released this week by CNN...

00:13:15.127 --> 00:13:16.762
Democracy can't function
that way.

00:13:16.762 --> 00:13:18.630
It depends on everyone
accepting the results.

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:20.799
The NFL would stink,
if the Jets declared themselves

00:13:20.799 --> 00:13:23.402
Super Bowl champions every year
they went 2 and 14,

00:13:23.402 --> 00:13:25.904
not to mention that, if they did
have the Lombardi Trophy,

00:13:25.904 --> 00:13:27.506
they would most certainly
fumble it.

00:13:27.506 --> 00:13:29.174
[ Laughter ]

00:13:29.174 --> 00:13:32.211
See? Fall comes and the Mets
come out of our focus.

00:13:32.211 --> 00:13:35.513
[ Laughter ]
The Jets come into our focus.

00:13:35.513 --> 00:13:37.949
Last night's landslide
repudiation of Trumpism

00:13:37.949 --> 00:13:40.519
in the country's most populous
state proved two things --

00:13:40.519 --> 00:13:43.856
Trumpism is deeply unpopular,
but it also still drives

00:13:43.856 --> 00:13:45.624
the Republican Party.
It's not going away.

00:13:45.624 --> 00:13:48.427
They can't win majorities
of voters the normal way,

00:13:48.427 --> 00:13:51.129
so they use anti-democratic
loopholes, instead.

00:13:51.129 --> 00:13:54.533
We have to fix the system
through major electoral reforms,

00:13:54.533 --> 00:13:56.468
fast, before Republicans
can take advantage again.

00:13:56.468 --> 00:13:59.471
Otherwise, Republicans could do
to democracy what they did

00:13:59.471 --> 00:14:01.607
to Mike Lindell's reputation
and...

00:14:01.607 --> 00:14:03.675
-Smash it in a million
different pieces.

00:14:03.675 --> 00:14:05.344
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:14:05.344 --> 00:14:08.814
♪♪

